<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  The repository addon. Installed ONCE from a zip; after that Kodi checks it on its own and offers every
  new version of IPTV Balkan without anyone copying a file anywhere.

  The three URLs below are the whole contract, and they must be plain, stable, direct-download links —
  which is exactly why this is not hosted on Google Drive. A Drive share link redirects, hands back an
  HTML confirmation page for anything sizeable, and changes its file id on every re-upload; Kodi asks for
  `addons.xml` and expects `addons.xml`, so all three of those break it. The files are served from a plain
  static host; if it ever changes, the three URLs above change with it and every existing install has
  to install the repository zip again — which is the one thing worth getting right the first time.

  If the folder on the server ever moves, the three URLs above have to be changed HERE, by hand, and
  `BASE_URL` in C:\Projects\kodi-iptvbox\pack.py has to be changed to match. This file is not generated:
  pack.py reads it (for the version) and zips it, and it builds `addons.xml` — the index — from it and
  from the addon's own manifest. The comment that used to sit here said the opposite, which would have
  cost somebody an afternoon of wondering why their edit "kept being undone".

  1.0.1 — THE VERSION WAS RAISED TO MIGRATE THE PEOPLE WHO WERE LEFT BEHIND.

  Until now two different files shipped under the SAME version 1.0.0. One sent Kodi to
  `raw.githubusercontent.com/darktvaddon/repo` (right); the other, still live on
  `iptvbox-player.com/kodi/`, sent it back to that server — which has been stuck on the add-on's
  1.23.0 since the move to GitHub. Anyone who installed the repository from the server has therefore
  received NO update at all, quietly: everything "works" on their box, it simply never changes.

  Kodi could not repair that by itself, and this is the part worth remembering: an add-on is only
  offered an update when the version NUMBER rises. Both files said 1.0.0, so there was nothing to
  offer — the wrong pointer was frozen in place by the very mechanism meant to fix it.

  Hence 1.0.1. Published to BOTH trees, the stale boxes see a newer repository, update it, and from
  that moment read GitHub. Once they have, the old channel can be retired.
-->
<addon id="repository.iptvbalkan"
       name="IPTV Balkan repozitorijum"
       version="1.0.1"
       provider-name="IPTV Balkan">
  <extension point="xbmc.addon.repository" name="IPTV Balkan">
    <dir>
      <info compressed="false">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/darktvaddon/repo/main/addons.xml</info>
      <checksum>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/darktvaddon/repo/main/addons.xml.md5</checksum>
      <datadir zip="true">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/darktvaddon/repo/main/</datadir>
    </dir>
  </extension>
  <extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
    <summary lang="en_GB">Source for the IPTV Balkan add-on — next: Add-ons → Install from repository → IPTV Balkan</summary>
    <description lang="en_GB">This is the SOURCE, not the add-on itself — which is why it has no screen to open.
Install the add-on with: Add-ons → Install from repository → IPTV Balkan repository → Video add-ons → IPTV Balkan → Install.
Every later version then arrives on its own.</description>
    <summary lang="sr_RS">Izvor za dodatak IPTV Balkan — sledeci korak: Dodaci → Instaliraj iz repozitorijuma → IPTV Balkan</summary>
    <description lang="sr_RS">Ovo je IZVOR, ne sam dodatak — zato se ne otvara i nema svoj ekran.
Dodatak se instalira ovako: Dodaci → Instaliraj iz repozitorijuma → IPTV Balkan repozitorijum → Video dodaci → IPTV Balkan → Instaliraj.
Posle toga sve nove verzije stizu same, bez ijednog zipa.</description>
    <platform>all</platform>
    <license>Proprietary</license>
    <assets>
      <icon>icon.png</icon>
    </assets>
  </extension>
</addon>
